# lowered from the probe emitx_two_values.json by the fixture lowering (private tooling)
# The lane runs `ds-formal-tests --fixture` on this and diffs against
# emitx_two.expected (scripts/formal/check_idris.py). LSCO.2.1's copy emit over TWO Trig
# values: the copied value decides which tuple each Result carries ("t1"
# is token 0, "t2" token 1: the blocks 3 and 11), so an emit that ignored the
# bound fact would give both Results one payload. Agrees with libds
# (idris_churn.py --fixtures on the probe).
schema 0 relation Trig
schema 1 explicit Result
alpha 0 0
alpha 1 1
rule 0 make_result
pattern 0 0 0
emitx 0 1 0 1 slot 0 key 0
step assert t1 0 1000000000000000000003 1
step assert t2 0 1000000000000000000011 1
step pump
step retract t1
step pump
